  "title": "Be Open to New Ideas, Even When They Challenge Old Beliefs",
  "description": "Be open to new ideas, even when they challenge old beliefs. Here’s how: - Question traditions: Ask, “Why do we do it this way? Could there be a better approach?” - Explore the evidence: Dive into new ideas with curiosity instead of rejection. - Adopt a beginner’s mindset: Treat every new concept as a chance to learn, not a threat to your experience. Example: If someone suggests a new tool or method at work, give it a fair try before dismissing it as unnecessary.",
